    "findings/test-case-check.md":
      "Reviewed head: d693e817590181d6ca31729995d507a6d2671aaa\n\n# Test case review\n\nScope: `test/cases/ARK-T16.md` and `test/cases/ARK-T17.md` at commit `d693e81`; test design only, no product or test-code diff review.\n\nNo findings.\n\n## Checks\n\n- **Real risk:** ARK-T16 protects role preservation, compatibility with projects that omit the optional roles, and refusal of a writer role without a model. ARK-T17 protects the copyable bootstrap configuration against invalid configuration and loss of reviewer vendor separation.\n- **No duplicates:** Compared the objectives and risks of existing local cases ARK-T1 through ARK-T15. None owns either new contract. ARK-T16 owns arbitrary project role loading; ARK-T17 owns the shipped bootstrap example and its vendor relationship, so its use of the same loader is not duplicate ownership.\n- **Integration boundary:** Both cases run a real `ark status` command against temporary project configuration and inspect actual `loadConfig` results. Neither proposes mocking the behavior under review or substituting a unit-only case.\n- **Required fields:** Both contain objective, preconditions, steps, expected results, technique, level, priority, risk, and screenshot checkpoints. A read-only Bun field/section check exited 0 and reported all six checked metadata fields and all five required sections present for each file. Screenshot checkpoints explicitly say none because these cases have no UI surface.\n- **AC1 / ARK-T16:** Covers both roles with exact configured harness/model values, neither optional role, and `test_writer` without a model with a nonzero CLI exit and a role-specific missing-model error. This matches `plan.yml` and the ticket's `verified_by` mapping.\n- **AC2 / ARK-T17:** Loads the actual default bootstrap roles block as configuration and checks that the test reviewer uses a different vendor from both implementer and writer. This matches the plan's automated proof. Documentation examples and the stop/escalate prose remain inspection obligations; this approval does not claim those changes are implemented or verified.\n- **No wording tests:** ARK-T17 parses executable configuration data rather than asserting prose strings. Neither case tests playbook/doc wording.\n\nVerification here is case inspection and the field/section check, not execution of the planned integration tests. Product implementation and runtime AC evidence belong to later steps.\n\nP0: 0, P1: 0, P2: 0, P3: 0.\n\n## Merge risk\n\n- Verification: good \u2014 case contents, criteria mapping, existing case objectives/risks, and required-field presence checked; implementation execution is outside this step.\n- Alignment: good \u2014 cases match the AC1/AC2 automated contracts without wording assertions.\n- Impact: good \u2014 this commit adds two test specifications only.\n- Rollback cost: good \u2014 case-only additions are straightforward to revise.\n- Door: two-way.\n- Blast radius: future role-config and bootstrap-example integration tests.\n\nVerdict: approve\n",
